          </zone>
          <zone fixed-size='412' forceUpdate='true' h='52500' id='5' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='99200' x='300' y='7125'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12' underline='true'>Filters / Parameters</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Region</run>
              <run>: Region to which the country belongs
</run>
              <run bold='true'>Country</run>
              <run>: country code &#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Last N days</run>
              <run>: Number of days over which the snapshot data is computed. For example if N days is set to 7, the number of DH customers is calculated looking at orders from the last 7 days.
</run>
              <run bold='true'>Ride time / Total Time: </run>
              <run>Whether to use only </run>
              <run bold='true'>ride time</run>
              <run> (near customer - pick up) or </run>
              <run bold='true'>total time </run>
              <run>(near customer - order creation) when calculating % of customers reached under T minutes and rendering the n-customers distribution
</run>
              <run bold='true'>Less than T:</run>
              <run>  T minutes used to calculate % of customers reached under T

</run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12' underline='true'>Metrics</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>All DH Customers: </run>
              <run>Number of customers that made an order through any DH service in the </run>
              <run bold='true'>last N days</run>
              <run>.&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Dmart Customers: </run>
              <run>Number of customers that made an order fulfilled through a </run>
              <run bold='true'>Dmart</run>
              <run> in the </run>
              <run bold='true'>last</run>
              <run>Æ </run>
              <run bold='true'>N days. </run>
              <run>% shown underneath is over </run>
              <run bold='true'>All DH Customers.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Reached under T: </run>
              <run>Customers who&apos;s average Dmart </run>
              <run bold='true'>Ride / Total Time </run>
              <run>is </run>
              <run bold='true'>less than T</run>
              <run> in the </run>
              <run bold='true'>last N days</run>
              <run>. The % shown underneath is over </run>
              <run bold='true'>All DH Customers.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12' underline='true'>Graphs</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Ride / Total Time distribution </run>
              <run>(1st graph)</run>
              <run bold='true'>:</run>
              <run>
For the customers with at least one Dmart order in the </run>
              <run bold='true'>last N days</run>
              <run>, which % falls into each time bucket. The more to the left, the faster we are fulfiling orders.

</run>
              <run bold='true'>Dmart Penetration </run>
              <run>(2nd graph):
N customers with a dmart order in the month / N customers with an order through any DH service in the month. Corresponds to the % under </run>
              <run bold='true'>Dmart Customers</run>
              <run> but may not coincide since here we calculate for the month, </run>
              <run bold='true'>not over the last N days.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
